--TEST--
an `autoload` in a file the map itself found does not compile — `rule:programs/autoload`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The map is fixed the moment it is first consulted, so a declaration in a
// file that consulting it loaded would extend the map that found the file —
// the map would depend on itself. Only the entry point's own `require` chain
// declares it.
require './src/Bootstrap.nvs';
echo App\Greeter::from(), "\n";
--FILE src/Bootstrap.nvs--
<?nvs
autoload 'App' from './';
--FILE src/Greeter.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace App;

// Reached only through the prefix above, so this line is refused rather than
// honored. It is not `E0317` as well: § 2 counts declarations, and an
// `autoload` is not one.
autoload 'Other' from '../other';

class Greeter
{
    public static function from(): string
    {
        return "App";
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0316]: `autoload` is not honored in a file reached by autoload
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
